
### using AES-CBC

* build

cmake -S src/ml -B build/tools
cmake --build build/tools


* encrypt a file

cd build/tools

KEY=1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234
IV=12345678901234567890123456789012

./encrypt <inputfile> <outputfile> $KEY $IV


* decrypt a file

./decrypt <inputfile> <outputfile> $KEY $IV


* verify with openssl

openssl enc -d -aes-256-cbc -nosalt \
  -K $KEY \
  -iv $IV \
  -in <inputfile.crypt> -out <outputfile.plain>


### using AES-GCM

```sh
KEY=1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234 && \
NONCE=123456789012345678901234 && \
rm -f test.gcm test.plain.gcm && \
./encryptGCM test.txt test.gcm $KEY $NONCE && \
./decryptGCM test.gcm test.plain.gcm $KEY $NONCE && \
diff test.txt test.plain.gcm && echo "diff: files are identical"
```
